     1                                  ;
     2                                  ; -------------------------------------
     3                                  ; -- Overview
     4                                  ; -------------------------------------
     5                                  ;
     6                                  ; This Forth interpreter is a stack-based, threaded system combining code and data
     7                                  ; in a single memory space. Its core is the dictionary, which stores all words
     8                                  ; (variables, constants, and executable primitives) as linked list entries. Each
     9                                  ; word contains pointers to its name, code, and optional data.
    10                                  
    11                                  ; The interpreter has two loops: the outer interpreter reads and parses input,
    12                                  ; managing compilation and execution flow, while the inner interpreter dispatches
    13                                  ; execution by following each word’s code field address (CFA). This design allows
    14                                  ; the system to be self-extending: new words can be defined at runtime, existing
    15                                  ; words can be altered, and the dictionary itself is both program and environment.
    16                                  
    17                                  ; Because this file implements the interpreter in assembly, definitions, variables,
    18                                  ; and primitives exist alongside executable code. With care, new Forth words can
    19                                  ; even execute additional assembly instructions. This powerful flexibility comes
    20                                  ; with complexity: program flow is intertwined with memory layout, initialization,
    21                                  ; and runtime code generation. Comments have been added to help clarify the system.
    22                                  
    23                                  ; The Forth dictionary is the heart of the interpreter: a self-describing mix of
    24                                  ; memory, code, and data, powering the two main loops. Each entry has four fields:
    25                                  
    26                                  ; +------+----------------------------------------------+
    27                                  ; | Field| Description                                  |
    28                                  ; +------+----------------------------------------------+
    29                                  ; | LFA  | Link Field Address: pointer to previous word |
    30                                  ; | NFA  | Name Field Address: pointer to word’s name   |
    31                                  ; | CFA  | Code Field Address: pointer to executable    |
    32                                  ; | DFA  | Data Field Address: variable/constant value  |
    33                                  ; +------+----------------------------------------------+
    34                                  
    35                                  ; The system runs by traversing these entries and executing code via the CFA.
    36                                  
    37                                  ; The system relies on 
    38                                  ; +-----------+-------------------------------+
    39                                  ; | Helper    | Description                   |
    40                                  ; +-----------+-------------------------------+
    41                                  ; | getchar   | read a character from input   |
    42                                  ; | outchar   | write a character to output   |
    43                                  ; | docolon   | execute a colon-defined word  |
    44                                  ; | dovar     | handle variable access        |
    45                                  ; | doconst   | handle constant access        |
    46                                  ; | next      | inner interpreter loop        |
    47                                  ; +-----------+-------------------------------+
    48                                  
    49                                  ; These, together with Forth Dictionary Words, form the complete system.
    50                                  
    51                                  ; +-------------------------------------------------------------------+
    52                                  ; | Forth Dictionary Words                                            |
    53                                  ; +---------+-----------+----------+-----------+----------+-----------+
    54                                  ; | state   | >in       | #tib     | dp        | base     | last      |
    55                                  ; | tib     | abort     | ,        | lit       | rot      | drop      |
    56                                  ; | dup     | swap      | +        | =         | @        | !         |
    57                                  ; | 0branch | branch    | execute  | exit      | count    | >number   |
    58                                  ; | accept  | word      | emit     | find      | :        | ;         |
    59                                  ; | (;code) | constant  | interpret|           |          |           |
    60                                  ; +---------+-----------+----------+-----------+----------+-----------+
    61                                  
    62                                  
    63                                  ; -------------------------------------
    64                                  ; -- Program Entry Point
    65                                  ; -------------------------------------
    66                                  
    67                                  org 0100h
    68 00000000 EB54                    jmp cfa_abort+2     ; jump to abort code start (initialize the program)
    69                                  
