   270                                  ; -------------------------------------
   271                                  ; -- Inner Interpreter (next)
   272                                  ; -- Forth Fetch-and-Execute Loop
   273                                  ; -------------------------------------
   274                                  
   275                                  ; --------------------------------------------------------------------
   276                                  ; This is the classic indirect threaded Forth inner interpreter, called “next.”
   277                                  ; Each Forth word’s definition consists of a list of code field addresses (cfa).
   278                                  ; next repeatedly fetches the next cfa and executes the code it points to.
   279                                  ;
   280                                  ; Each word’s code executes, then typically returns to next to process the next cfa.
   281                                  ; This dispatch loop is the core of the Forth execution model.
   282                                  ;
   283                                  ; Startup behavior:
   284                                  ;   si is initialized to cfa_interpret+2 and execution jumps to next.
   285                                  ;   This skips fetching interpret’s own cfa.
   286                                  ;   The first lodsw fetches the cfa of the first word in interpret’s thread
   287                                  ;   and jumps to it, entering the interpreter loop directly.
   288                                  ;
   289                                  ; The next routine appears here among the word definitions because it is
   290                                  ; part of the runtime environment and is referenced like any other word.
   291                                  ; Placing it here allows references to its address to be resolved during the build
   292                                  ; and ensures it participates in the threaded code sequence.
   293                                  ; --------------------------------------------------------------------
   294                                  
   295 000000EF AD                      next:               lodsw               ; load word at [si] into ax, increment si by 2
   296 000000F0 97                                          xchg di,ax          ; di now holds the fetched cfa
   297 000000F1 FF25                                        jmp word[di]        ; indirect jump to the cfa
   298                                  
   299                                  ; -------------------------------------
   300                                  ; -- Interpreter-Dependent Primitives
   301                                  ; -- Require the inner interpreter to execute via cfa
   302                                  ; -------------------------------------
   303                                  ; These primitives rely on the inner interpreter being active to fetch
   304                                  ; and execute code field addresses (cfa) of words.
   305                                  
